> why do you use tr "\n" "," | sed 's/.$//' to construct the instmods s=
tring?

In some cases there could be an alias representing more than one module=
 like as
follows
# modprobe -R pci:v00008086d000024D0sv00000000sd00000000bc06sc01i00
intel_rng
lpc_ich

In such cases, we need to convert the above output of `modprobe -R` int=
o the
format like intel_rng,lpc_ich, so that we can ask instmods to install a=
ll of them.

~Pratyush
